  "description": "Below is the configuration for the new user\u2011profile form that will be rendered as a tabbed wizard. The wizard uses the identifier **armsTabHeader** for its tab headers and pulls its step definitions from **wizard-definitions/arms-draft.json**. The form concludes with the standard footer template named **standard\u2011footer**.\n\nThe first tab, titled **User Information**, contains two input fields. The \u201cfirst name\u201d field is a simple text box that displays the placeholder \u201cEnter first name\u201d and carries the CSS class **input\u2011lg**. It receives initial focus via the element ID **firstNameInput** and is mandatory; validation is tied to **firstNameValidation**, with the message \u201cFirst name is required.\u201d The second field, \u201cbio\u201d, is a textarea configured with 50 columns and 5 rows, styled with the class **textarea\u2011md**. Its focus ID is **bioTextarea**, it is also required, and its validation ID **bioValidation** will show the notice \u201cBiography cannot be empty.\u201d when left blank.\n\nThe second tab, labeled **Settings**, holds a single complex field named **preferences**. Its configuration includes a key/value pair of **key1** set to **value1**, and it is styled with the class **settings\u2011section**. The section gains focus through **preferencesSection**; although no save\u2011rules are defined for it, the validation ID **preferencesValidation** is prepared to emit the message \u201cPreferences must be set.\u201d if needed."
